    "app.priv.titulo": "Privacy and cookies", "app.priv.enlace": "Privacy and cookies", "app.priv.ver": "See the policy",
    "app.priv.fecha": "Last updated: 10 November 2026 (resident accounts)",
    "app.priv.resumen": "Yaguachi Weather uses no tracking or advertising cookies and no third-party analytics. It only stores on your phone what it needs to work, even without signal.",
    "app.priv.aviso": "Yaguachi Weather uses no tracking or advertising cookies. It only stores on your phone what it needs to work (your place, language and the latest data).",
    "app.priv.entendido": "Got it",
    "app.priv.resp.t": "Who is responsible",
    "app.priv.resp.c": "Yaguachi Weather is an <b>independent project</b>. It is not an official channel of the cantonal COE, the Risk Management Secretariat or INAMHI.",
    "app.priv.cookies.t": "Cookies",
    "app.priv.cookies.c": "The app does not set its own cookies to track you or show ads, and it uses no third-party analytics tools. That's why we don't ask you to accept cookies.",
    "app.priv.local.t": "What is stored on your phone",
    "app.priv.local.c": "We use the browser's local storage (these are not cookies and they don't leave your phone except what you send):<ul><li><b>A random identifier</b> for the phone, to recognise your reports and your likes.</li><li>If you sign in with your <b>account</b>, your name (without ID number or email), to show it in «My account».</li><li><b>Your place</b> (community, street or location) and your <b>language</b>.</li><li>Your <b>map preferences</b> (layers and background) and the Neighbours filter.</li><li><b>Reports waiting to be sent</b> if there was no signal.</li><li><b>The latest data you downloaded</b> (levels, alerts, territory) to see it offline.</li><li>That you have seen this notice.</li><li>If you turned on notifications, this phone&#39;s <b>notification identifier</b>.</li></ul>",
    "app.priv.cache.t": "Offline use",
    "app.priv.cache.c": "A service worker keeps the app's files, the map layers and the map areas you have already seen, so the app opens even without signal.",
    "app.priv.terceros.t": "Third-party services",
    "app.priv.terceros.c": "<ul><li>The map is drawn with <b>OpenStreetMap</b> and, if you choose satellite, <b>Esri</b>: when it loads they receive your phone's IP address, like any website.</li><li>If you turn on <b>notifications</b>, your phone registers with <b>Firebase Cloud Messaging</b> (Google) to receive alerts with the app closed: Google receives a notification identifier and the phone&#39;s IP address. We store that identifier with the chosen community, the language and the approximate phone type (system and browser), nothing else.</li><li>If you ask for the <b>route to a shelter</b>, your location (rounded to about 10 m) goes to our server, which asks <b>OpenStreetMap Germany (FOSSGIS)</b> for the way: that service does not receive your phone&#39;s IP address. We do not store your location. If you tap <b>Go with Google Maps</b>, Google Maps opens with the destination and its policy applies there.</li><li><b>App use:</b> while you use it, at most every 6 hours, the app tells the server that this phone is using it: the phone's encrypted signature, the approximate type (for example «Android · Chrome»), the brand (for example Samsung; never the model, which does not leave your phone), the system version (for example Android 14), whether it is a phone, tablet or computer, whether it is installed, the language and the app version. That way the team knows how many phones use it. Only the superadmin sees the list, by code and without names, and it is deleted after 6 months without use.</li><li><b>Reach of alerts and incidents:</b> when you open an alert or an incident from the risk team, the app counts it so the team knows how many phones it reached. Only a one-way encrypted signature of the phone identifier is stored (not the identifier, your name or your location) plus the approximate phone type (for example «Android · Chrome»). The team sees numbers. Only the superadmin can see the list of phones by code (for example «7F3A2C»), with that approximate type and, if you turned on notifications, the community and language: never your name, phone number or location. Every lookup is recorded.</li><li><b>Storms nearby:</b> our server fetches the satellite images, lightning and next-hour rain from NASA, Unidata and Open-Meteo. Your phone does not connect to them or send them anything.</li><li>If you tap <b>Share</b>, <b>Facebook</b> or <b>WhatsApp</b> opens; their own policies and cookies apply there.</li></ul>",
    "app.priv.reportes.t": "Your reports",
    "app.priv.reportes.c": "When you send a report we store what you write, the location, the photos if you attach them (up to 3), your account (if you sent it with one), the phone identifier and the IP address it was sent from (only to stop abuse, for example many reports in a row; it is deleted after 48 hours). If the analyst discards a report, its photos are deleted right away. Your name, ID number and photo are not published. Other people's photos are only published if the analyst verifies the report, and all photos are deleted after 90 days. We do this with your consent, under Ecuador's Organic Law on Personal Data Protection.",
    "app.priv.derechos.t": "Your rights",
    "app.priv.derechos.c": "You can delete what the app stored on this phone at any time with the button below. You delete your account yourself from «My account». To ask for access to, correction or deletion of a report you sent, contact the Yaguachi Weather team.",
    "app.priv.borrar.t": "Delete this phone's data",
    "app.priv.borrar.c": "Deletes your place, language, preferences, pending reports and the offline copy. Reports you already sent stay on the server, but this phone will no longer recognise them as yours.",
    "app.priv.borrar.btn": "Delete this phone's data", "app.priv.borrar.confirmar": "Tap again to confirm",
